<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-1327] Height parameter in z.show python interpreter does not take effect for PNG images</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-1327</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Height parameter in z.show() function in python interpreter does not take effect for PNG images. It can be tested as follows:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; matplotlib.pyplot as plt

x = [1,2,3,4,5]
y = [6,7,8,9,0]

plt.plot(x, y, marker=&lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;o&quot;&lt;/span&gt;)
z.show(plt, fmt=&lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;png&quot;&lt;/span&gt;, height=&lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;250px&quot;&lt;/span&gt;)
plt.close()
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="12997207">ZEPPELIN-1327</key>
