                            <comment id="15422221" author="bzz" created="Tue, 16 Aug 2016 05:43:34 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=pbustios&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;pbustios&quot;&gt;pbustios&lt;/a&gt; Thank you for catching this one! &lt;br/&gt;
Same as with &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-1328&quot; title=&quot;z.show in python interpreter does not display PNG images in python 3&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;ZEPPELIN-1328&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;ZEPPELIN-1328&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; - please let me know if you have a plan to address this guy or do you think we should ask &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=agoodman&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;agoodman&quot;&gt;agoodman&lt;/a&gt; for help?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;These both issues make me think - we did not pay attention or prioritize python3 compatibility in Zeppelin so far. &lt;br/&gt;
Should we do that? It means we going to need at least a separate CI profile, to run the tests on both versions. What do you think?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15422313" author="agoodman" created="Tue, 16 Aug 2016 06:45:40 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=bzz&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;bzz&quot;&gt;bzz&lt;/a&gt; I don&apos;t think this is a python3 issue, it&apos;s probably a bug in the HTML formatting string in the code. Specifically this line in &lt;tt&gt;bootstrap.py&lt;/tt&gt; should have the comma removed:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;            html = &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;%html &amp;lt;img src={img} width={width}, height={height}&amp;gt;&quot;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I do in fact know that I at least tested this originally with just width, so it&apos;s understandable that I missed this too.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15422378" author="bzz" created="Tue, 16 Aug 2016 07:58:55 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;You are right, it&apos;s not related to python3 at all, and thank you for catching and explaning this subtle bug in original python interpreter implementation!&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15423038" author="pbustios" created="Tue, 16 Aug 2016 16:52:07 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Indeed, the issue is caused by the comma.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
