                            <comment id="15431957" author="githubbot" created="Tue, 23 Aug 2016 01:44:25 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Github user bzz commented on the issue:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/1352&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/1352&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    @bustios thank you for the fix and followup on CI!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    Could you please also briefly explain, why Python3 compatibility facilities are not required here any more?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15432014" author="githubbot" created="Tue, 23 Aug 2016 02:33:46 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Github user bustios commented on the issue:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/1352&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/1352&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    Yes @bzz, I just deleted `if self.py3:` but not `img_str = img_str.decode(&apos;ascii&apos;)` (it is in line 173), which means it will be executed for both Python 2 and 3. Decoding bytes to string it necessary for Python 3 because that version makes distinction between String and Bytes, which does not occur in Python 2.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    Maybe, `img_str = img_str.decode(&apos;ascii&apos;)` should be in a separate line of code to be clear.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15432122" author="githubbot" created="Tue, 23 Aug 2016 04:33:17 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Github user bzz commented on the issue:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/1352&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/1352&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    Got it, makes perfect sense! &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    Do you think we should add a comment in there, explaining that compatibility is the reason for such decoding? I feel like this might help future contributors to see how to deal with such compatibility issue.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    Other then that - it looks great to me, thanks again for fixing! It shall be ready to merge to master right after that, if there is no further discussion.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15433028" author="githubbot" created="Tue, 23 Aug 2016 15:33:59 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Github user bustios commented on the issue:&lt;/p&gt;

